 "shapes": [
  "MQBR MQBRCIH: CALL 'MQPUT' USING ... WS-MSGLEN WS-MSG ..., 01 WS-MSG = 05 WS-CIH (COPY MQBCIH, the 180-byte MQCIH version 2 stand-in) + WS-COMMAREA X(40); MQCIH Format set to the COMMAREA's format name, LinkType program, UOWControl only"
 ],
 "asserts": "MQBRCIH's MQPUT CALL is one call_sites fact (form literal, resolves_to null) with a call edge from 0000-MAIN and a gaps entry. The 01 group WS-MSG holds WS-CIH (copy_members MQBCIH, whose 38 fields total 180 bytes, the length IBM gives MQCIH_LENGTH_2, with StrucLength VALUE 180 and Version VALUE 2) followed by the 40-character WS-COMMAREA, and WS-MSGLEN is 180 + 40 = 220; the key's layouts fact for WS-MSG is 220 bytes. The key asserts the layout only: it does not model the bridge.",
